<%#
  Filter bar. Collapsed behind a Filters button, with the filters that are set shown beside it as
  chips. A plain (borderless) bar sits 16px above the results it filters.

    render "shared/essentials/filter_bar", url: donations_path, frame: "donations-results" do
      <div class="min-w-0"> ... one filter ... </div>
    end

  Filters submit with GET, so a filtered view stays a shareable, bookmarkable URL.

  Options:

    frame:              The id of the turbo_frame_tag wrapping the results. With it the bar
                        applies on change and replaces only the results; without it the bar
                        submits normally and keeps its Filter button.

    auto_submit: true   Apply on change without a frame -- a full page reload per change. Only
                        for a bar that has no results frame to update.

    clear_path:         Where "Clear all" goes. Defaults to the current path.

    in_card: true       The bar belongs to a tab rather than to the page: it renders inside the
                        card, under the tab strip, with the card's own padding and a rule under
                        it. **This is what keeps a tab strip still.** With the bar above the card,
                        a tab that has filters and a tab that does not put the strip at two
                        different heights -- measured at 228 and 174 on Partner agencies, a 54px
                        jump on every switch, reported as "the card jumps up and down". Put the
                        frame around the *table* rather than around the card, so applying a filter
                        does not re-render the strip.

  Every cell inside the block is `min-w-0` and holds one filter: the grid gives them equal
  columns, and a long option truncates rather than pushing its column past its share.

  The Filter button exists only for the no-JS case. It is hidden in the markup and restored by a
  <noscript> rule -- hiding it from JavaScript on connect meant it was painted and then removed a
  frame later, which flashed on every load.
%>
<% clear_path ||= request.path %>
<% frame = local_assigns[:frame] %>
<%# A bar pointed at a frame always applies on change: that is the whole reason for the frame. %>
<% auto_submit = frame.present? || local_assigns.fetch(:auto_submit, false) %>
<%
  # Every bar collapses, whatever its size. This was a threshold -- five filters or more -- and
  # two behaviours across sixteen pages is worse than one whichever one it is: learning the
  # filter bar on donations and then meeting something else on transfers teaches nothing
  # transferable.
  controls = capture { yield }
  panel_id = "filter-panel-#{SecureRandom.uuid}"

  controllers = ["disclosure", "filter-summary"]
  form_data = {}
  if auto_submit
    controllers.unshift("auto-submit")
    form_data[:action] = "change->auto-submit#submit input->auto-submit#debounce"
  end
  form_data[:controller] = controllers.join(" ")
  if frame.present?
    form_data[:turbo_frame] = frame
    # Turbo Drive is off app-wide, and Turbo only ignores that for elements *inside* a frame.
    # This form targets one from outside it, so without an explicit opt-in Turbo declines to
    # handle the submit and the browser does a full page reload instead -- silently, because
    # the filter still works. See Session#elementIsNavigatable.
    form_data[:turbo] = true
  end
%>
<%
  # A bar above a card is spaced from it; a bar inside one is bounded by it.
  in_card = local_assigns.fetch(:in_card, false)
  bar_class = in_card ? "border-b border-slate-200 px-5 py-4" : "mb-4"
%>
<%= form_tag url, method: :get, class: bar_class, data: form_data do %>
  <% if frame.present? %>
    <%#
      Applying into a frame changes nothing a screen reader notices -- no navigation, no focus
      move. This is the announcement, and it lives out here rather than in the results because a
      live region has to survive the swap: an aria-live element that is itself replaced does not
      announce its new contents.
    %>
    <p class="sr-only" role="status" data-auto-submit-target="status"></p>
  <% end %>
  <% if auto_submit %>
    <%# Without JavaScript nothing submits the form on change, so the button has to come back. %>
    <noscript>
      <style>.filter-bar-submit { display: inline-flex !important; }</style>
    </noscript>
  <% end %>
  <%#
    A grid, not a flex row. A flex item sizes to its content -- the longest option in the menu
    -- so `flex-wrap` with min-width boxes gave six different control widths across four pages
    (208 to 289px) and packed each line to the left, leaving 337px, 793px and 852px of ragged
    space at the ends. Equal columns fix both: the width follows the breakpoint, not the text.

    Cells are `min-w-0` so a long option cannot push a column past its share; the select
    truncates instead.
  %>
  <%#
    The panel starts closed, and stays closed even when the page arrives filtered: the chips
    beside the button already say what is applied, and opening automatically would give the space
    back on exactly the pages where it was worth saving.
  %>
  <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
    <button type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="<%= panel_id %>"
            data-action="click->disclosure#toggle" data-filter-toggle
            <%# A secondary button, and it had drifted from one: `font-semibold` and a `shadow-sm`
                that no other secondary button in the app carries. That is the cost of a pasted
                class string, so it asks the helper for them now. %>
            class="<%= essentials_button_classes(variant: :secondary) %>">
      <i class="bi-funnel" aria-hidden="true"></i>Filters
      <span class="inline-flex h-5 min-w-5 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-brand-600 px-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-white"
            data-filter-summary-target="count" hidden></span>
      <i class="bi-chevron-down text-slate-400 transition-transform" data-disclosure-chevron aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
    <%# `contents` so the chips are laid out by the row above, not boxed inside a wrapper. %>
    <div class="contents" data-filter-summary-target="chips"></div>
    <%= link_to "Clear all", clear_path,
          class: "text-sm font-medium text-brand-700 hover:underline",
          data: {filter_summary_target: "clear"}, hidden: true %>
  </div>

  <div id="<%= panel_id %>"
       class="hidden grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4">
    <%= controls %>
    <%#
      An ordinary grid cell, so it follows the last filter instead of taking a row of its own.
      `col-span-full` cost a row on every page with a bar, including the ones with a single
      filter. `self-end` sits it on the controls' baseline; the cells themselves are top-aligned
      because the date range grows downwards when Custom is chosen.

      There is no "Clear filters" here. "Clear all" sits with the chips above, which is where you
      are looking when you decide you have narrowed too far -- and one inside the panel is
      invisible exactly when the panel is shut. The submit button only exists for the no-JS case.
    %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 self-end">
      <button type="submit"
              class="filter-bar-submit <%= essentials_button_classes(variant: :primary, size: :md) %>"
              <%= tag.attributes(style: "display:none") if auto_submit %>>
        <i class="bi-funnel" aria-hidden="true"></i>Filter
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
